Try on every piece of blessed and uncursed armor to see if it's enchanted
with bonuses (especially if it came off the watch captain :). If a
shopkeeper offers you an abnormally large price for an item, you can bet
it's got plusses. 

Walking out of minetown with good naked AC requires walking in with a lot
of gold or coming up with plenty while you're there. A priest can tell you
more about it.

> Also, he was given Cleaver after #offering quite a number of critters to
> Crom and I read a few Enchant Weapon scrolls on it.  It glowed blue but
> in my inventory it still lists as rustproof battle-axe named Cleaver. Is
> it not possible to enchant artifacts?

If you don't know the initial enchantment, you won't know the result;
you'll still need an ID scroll. But you can #name the item ("ench twice"
for instance) to note that you've enchanted it yourself. If you've read "a
few", though, you should definitely stop now until you ID it. It could go
byebye next time.

